# Code ownership. The subsystem boundaries are described in CONTRACTS.md §5.
#
# A CODEOWNERS entry means "this person's review is required", not "only this
# person may change it". Later rules win, so the most specific rule for a path
# is the one that applies.
#
# A personal repository has no GitHub teams, so every path resolves to the
# maintainer. Split these into team handles when there are teams to point at —
# an entry naming a team that does not exist silently requests no review at all.

# Fallback: anything not claimed below.
*                                   @thesvj

